  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "AR41-001",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "category": "wrong-behavior",
      "artifact": "src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Data/RepositoryProfilingCoordinator.cs",
      "location": "lines 262-270",
      "affected_requirement": "Story AC-8; Spec User Story 3 scenario 2, FR-015, and SC-003; plan lines 132-135",
      "evidence": "The accepted contract requires the authorised SystemOwner to receive `仓库克隆失败：{details}` with secret-safe details. The coordinator instead hard-codes and persists `仓库克隆失败，请检查仓库地址和访问权限。`, discarding the required details form. RepositoryProfilingTests.cs lines 259-318 explicitly lock in this different message, so the mismatch is implemented and tested rather than an evidence omission.",
      "correction_outcome": "On clone or update failure, return and persist `仓库克隆失败：{sanitized details}` while excluding credentials and source content; update acceptance coverage to assert both the required prefix/details contract and redaction."
    },
    {
      "id": "AR41-002",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "category": "missing-behavior",
      "artifact": "src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Data/RepositoryProfilingCoordinator.cs",
      "location": "lines 337-349",
      "affected_requirement": "Story AC-7; Spec User Story 3 scenario 1, FR-014, and SC-003",
      "evidence": "The provider error containing `CodeGraph CLI not found` is used only to select ProviderUnavailable. The subsequent Error log receives the Chinese display string `本地 CodeGraph 服务不可用，请联系管理员。`; the required literal marker is never passed to the logger. RepositoryProfilingTests.cs lines 2603-2655 use NullLogger and assert only the user/persistence outcome, leaving the required log behavior unproven and absent.",
      "correction_outcome": "Emit an Error-level log containing the literal `CodeGraph CLI not found` and bounded non-sensitive context while preserving the clear Simplified-Chinese user message; add captured-logger acceptance coverage."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "REVISE: the pinned implementation substantially covers extraction, filtering, structural persistence, atomic provider failure, observability, authorization, and the mandatory real-provider contract gate, but it does not fully satisfy AC-7 or AC-8. Two required failure contracts are demonstrably missing or replaced in production code and tests."
}
